## The superseded generation is no longer effective

A generic 422 for a missing admission does not prove staleness, so the regression
pauses the ticket again and attempts a resume with the previous admission
(lease-item3-e2e / 2000000000003) after the ticket has accepted
lease-item3-running / 2000000000004:

  POST /bridge/v1/tickets/eb8f95ad49e3c1bcbe301697b4f6a54a/resume
    {"operationId":"...","admission":{"leaseId":"lease-item3-e2e","fencingToken":"2000000000003"}}
  HTTP 409
  {"error":"The execution lease admission is older than the generation this ticket already accepted",
   "code":"admissionStale","values":{}}

GET after the rejected resume:
{
  "state": "stopped",
  "assignmentId": "0e4b36d76caa8bacdb2c8858c2d62d49",
  "admission": {"leaseId":"lease-item3-running","fencingToken":"2000000000004"}
}
No new assignment, no admission change. The dedicated `admissionStale` code is what
distinguishes a superseded generation from a caller that supplied no admission.

