## Verdict

The path is observable: choose the first option (read the actual fence at
GET /bridge/v1/tickets/:id, corroborated by ticket.state_changed leaseId/fencingToken).
The old generation is rejected (409 `admissionStale`) and cannot become effective; pause evidence and the
running new assignment are asserted, so the previous "admission=null" limitation no longer
applies to the admission-aware runtime. Item 3 accepted.

Correction (M5-B matrix pass): the summary line above used to read "422", which contradicted the
captured response in the same log (`HTTP 409`, `"code":"admissionStale"`). A 422 is what a caller
without any admission gets; a superseded generation gets the dedicated 409. The raw output above is
unchanged.
